Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the GamePad's picture for the remote touch screen

The remote touch screen (PS5CEMU-HAR #38, from dolphin78's prototype)
shows the GamePad in a browser on the local network, whether or not the
TV shows it. While a browser shows it, the port asks for a picture at
most 30 times a second (PS5Cemu_StreamWantFrame): the GamePad's scan
buffer is brought up to date as the TV's would be, read back with the
screenshot's own path, and handed to the port (PS5Cemu_StreamFrame)
instead of saved. A screenshot asked for meanwhile is left alone.

The readback now ends the open render pass before its copies, makes
the buffer's writes visible to the host before it is read, waits on
the command buffer it submitted, and sizes the RGB buffer for formats
that were copied into an empty one.
